es associated to him are: Ze thang, Grwa thang and rMog po ([647FFPZR]: 545, based on [Q3KCZX7B]: 38).&#13;
Remembered for thirteen distinguished objects (such as royal insignia and religious articles), which could be objects of his clan ([4LDAV8UH]: 95.).</note></person><person xml:id="person3816"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar byang chub ye shes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨར་བྱང་ཆུབ་ཡེ་ཤེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang chub ye shes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang ye</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">a ro byang chub ye shes</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1056-12-31">after 1054 before 1056</birth><death notBefore="1134-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1134 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2552</idno><idno type="APIS">3816</idno><note type="comment">Dates according to [2V6H2FBU]: 24, n. 70 ("Since Ar was invited as a dge bshes to a monastery in 1076, it is hard to believe that he was not at least 20 years old, which would put his birth-date at least in 1056. The last trace of his existence is in 1144 when he took over the head of rgyal lha khang.").</note></person><person xml:id="person3834"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya dmar ba byang chub grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱ་དམར་བ་བྱང་ཆུབ་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lung rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lungs rgya dmar pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dam pa stod lung pa rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod rgya</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1075-12-31">after 1054 before 1075</birth><death notBefore="1135-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1135 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4749</idno><idno type="APIS">3834</idno><note type="comment">Floruit 1095–1135. [YF8Z2ZGH]: 332 "rGya dmar pa was not only fully learned, but also possessed numerous Tantric secret precepts."</note></person><person xml:id="person4235"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu ston brtson 'grus g.yung drung</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཁུ་སྟོན་བརྩོན་འགྲུས་གཡུང་དྲུང</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu brtson 'grus g.yung drung</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu ston chen po brtson 'grus g.yung drung</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu lha sdings pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu chen po lha sdings pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">khu ston shes rab brtson 'grus</persName><birth notBefore="1011-01-01" notAfter="1011-12-31">1011</birth><death notBefore="1075-01-01" notAfter="1075-12-31">1075</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3464</idno><idno type="APIS">4235</idno><note type="comment">The Abhidharma lineage found in (ID:5483) names "khu lha sdings pa brtson 'grus g.yung drung" between "gar mi yon tan g.yung drung" (ID:4234) and "rgya rgyal bu tshul le" (ID:4238). &#13;
The lineage in work (ID:5264) places him between " 'gar mi yon tan g.yung drung" (ID:4234) and both "ra" (ID:4237) and "rgya" (ID:4238).&#13;
&#13;
We consider "khu lha sdings pa" to be the same person as "khu ston brtson 'grus g.yung drung," who founded lHa sdings (ID:6701) in Yar lung.&#13;
&#13;
